// TEMPLATE: service layer skeleton — shared by ALL four framework reference
// types (resource / data source / action / ephemeral resource).
//
// Location: tencentcloud/services/<product>/service_tencentcloud_<product>.go
// If the file already exists (SDKv2 or framework references of the same
// product), APPEND the new service struct and methods to it instead of
// creating a new file.
//
// Golden rules (see the shipped example
// tencentcloud/services/antiddos/service_tencentcloud_antiddos.go):
//   1. SDK calls NEVER appear directly in framework lifecycle methods
//      (Create/Read/Update/Delete/Invoke/Open...). Every API call is wrapped
//      in a service method with retry + logging.
//   2. HARD RULE — ONE parameter standard for every lifecycle verb
//      (create/read/update/delete, data-source queries, action invokes):
//      the resource file builds the SDK request (schema get -> request
//      aggregation, or id -> request for read/delete), initializes the
//      service (New<Thing>Service(r.Client())), and calls
//      service.<Method>(ctx, request). NEVER loose parameters; NEVER build
//      schema-driven requests inside the service layer. The caller picks
//      its own item from a describe list; "no match in the list" is
//      not-found.
//   3. Read APIs retry with tccommon.ReadRetryTimeout, write APIs with
//      tccommon.WriteRetryTimeout. ALL retry lives in the service layer.
//   4. Call ratelimit.Check(request.GetAction()) before the retry loop.
//   5. Failures are logged with the "[CRITAL]" prefix (repo convention,
//      spelling included) carrying logId / action / request body / reason.
//   6. "Not found" is reported as (nil, nil): the caller treats a nil result
//      as not-found instead of an error. Describe methods return the FULL
//      list, shared by resource reads and data-source queries alike.

